      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i need help making sense of something. yesterday when the S&P dipped suddenly around 2pm, i felt this massive spike in my chest, like my heart rate just went through the roof before the news even hit the wires. it's happened a few times now where my body reacts literally seconds before a major volatility spike. is there any way the market's high frequency stuff could be reacting to biological signals or some kind of bio-frequency? it feels too consistent to be a coincidence.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
