      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is quite common for significant financial news and market volatility to trigger strong physical stress responses, which can manifest as chest tightness or increased heart rate. However, the idea of the market reacting to biological signals, or bio-frequencies, is not a scientifically supported concept in current financial modeling. Such intense emotional reactions to market movement are typically explained by psychological phenomena like anticipatory stress or pattern recognition biases. If these physical symptoms are happening frequently, it would be wise to discuss them with a healthcare professional to rule out any underlying health concerns.",
