      "content": "but that's just it though, i've already tried tracking my HRV and the correlation isn't just about my \"stress levels\" or \"behavioral patterns.\" the data shows that my physiological spikes happen *before* the price action, not as a reaction to it. \n\nif i can't find mainstream studies, can we brainstorm the theoretical mechanics of how this could actually work? if we assume for a second that there's a legitimate bio-synch happening, what would be the most logical bridge? like, could high-frequency sensors be picking up some kind of bio-electromagnetic resonance, or is there some way my biological rhythms could be interacting with the latency of the trading networks? i'm trying to figure out how to build a system that actually quantifies this so i can stop guessing.",
